# Derived outputs -- all regenerable from original/ plus the correction masks.
results/
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Written as `figures/` this matched at EVERY level, including
# crack_export/analysis/figures/, which holds 22 tracked deliverables. Already-tracked files
# are unaffected, but a newly generated figure there was silently un-addable -- `git add` said
# nothing and the file simply never arrived.
/figures/
fusion_cache/
removed_images/
training_data/*.png
training_data/*_cracks.csv
interior_active_learning/paint/*_paint_template.png
interior_active_learning/paint/*_painted.png
interior_active_learning/candidates/*_quicklook.png

# Sidebar thumbnail cache -- regenerated on demand from the paint templates,
# which are themselves derived. Without this rule every image you open leaves an
# untracked file behind in git status.
interior_active_learning/paint/.thumbs/

# The undo stack: per-session snapshots of the correction mask, bounded to 10 deep
# and consumed as you press Cmd-Z. Transient by design, and it would otherwise show
# up as untracked noise next to the labels that do matter.
interior_active_learning/paint/.undo/

# Build artifacts of a retrain: train_v3_weighted.py writes the candidate model,
# and the retrain gate writes the rollback copy. Committing them meant the model
# dropdown showed three names for one identical file.
models/crack_classifier_v3_weighted.joblib
models/crack_classifier_PREV.joblib
models/crack_classifier_replaced_*.joblib
models/crack_classifier_PRE_V3_BACKUP.joblib

# original/ IS tracked here, unlike in the research project: without the images a
# clone can retrain from the shipped labels but cannot reproduce a single overlay.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.upload_*

# Test scratch. The suite uploads synthetic images named apptest_*, and other
# probes use SELFTEST_/MASKGUARD_ prefixes. A `git add -A` after a test run
# committed three fake 400x600 images into original/ and published them, where
# they showed up in every user's image list as if they were data.
original/apptest*
original/SELFTEST*
original/MASKGUARD*
interior_active_learning/paint/apptest*
interior_active_learning/paint/SELFTEST*
interior_active_learning/paint/MASKGUARD*
.test_tmp/

# Experiment scratch: pickled pipeline stages, ~400 MB per image.
# Regenerated on demand by cheap_proposers.cached_case().
.proposal_cache/

# Timestamped model backups written by the retrain promote path. Local recovery
# artifacts, one per promotion -- not history worth shipping.
models/crack_classifier_PREV-*.joblib

# 223 MB of superseded overlay PNGs, kept locally as a recovery copy after the archive-model
# swap. Regenerable by the pipeline, and the archived repo still holds the originals, so
# there is no reason for every clone to pay for them.
archive/templates_before_archive_swap/

# Derived per-crack measurements. Regenerated by crack_measurements.py, and they churn on
# every run, so they are not history.
interior_active_learning/measurements/

# Regenerated by round3_margin_maximization.py and 50 MB on disk. It was committed
# once, was read by nothing, and has been purged from history; this keeps a re-run
# from putting it back.
interior_active_learning/code/experiments/round3_margin_maximization_full_grid.csv

# Derived outputs of the experiment scripts. Running an experiment should not dirty
# the tree: the figures are regenerated from the tracked result JSONs, and the
# dot-prefixed joblibs are per-run model caches.
interior_active_learning/benchmark_figures/
interior_active_learning/benchmark_figures_unified/
interior_active_learning/code/experiments/.*_model_*.joblib

# Local editor/agent scratch state and its worktrees. 2.5 GB here, and it was kept out of
# `git status` only by .git/info/exclude -- which is local to one machine and does not
# travel with a clone, so every collaborator would have seen it as untracked.
.claude/

# 2026-09-15 MAR 247 hydrogen batch: 80 frames (AS/HIP x H/ambient, 3x3 grid per cell),
# 3.7 GB, copied into original/ so the app can work with them but deliberately NOT released
# -- the repo is already a 2.4 GB clone. Provenance for every one of them, including the
# name it had in the capture folder, is in original/MANIFEST_260915_hydrogen.json (also
# untracked). Drop these rules if the batch is ever published.
original/MAR_H_*.tif
original/MAR_AmbB_*.tif
original/MANIFEST_260915_hydrogen.json
